Clinical Course: The muscle cramps and irregular heartbeat will resolve once the hospital safely replaces your potassium intravenously; long-term psychiatric support is required for the underlying disorder.

SAFETY-NETTING ADVICE

Do not get out of bed for any reason. If you feel sudden, severe chest pain or feel like you are going to black out, tell your parents immediately while waiting for the paramedics.

PATIENT EDUCATION

Treatment Explanation: Vomiting severely depletes your body of potassium, a salt that acts as the electrical wiring for your heart and muscles. Your current cramps and irregular heartbeat mean your electrical system is failing, which is why we must get you to the hospital for intravenous replacement immediately.
Actionable Steps: Stay completely still to reduce the workload on your heart. Be completely honest with the hospital doctors about how much you have purged so they can calculate the exact life-saving dose of potassium you need.

